  "Question": "Find the coordinates of the intersection of the lines $y=2x-1$ and $y=-x+5$. (Write the x-coordinate followed by the y-coordinate, separated by a comma.)",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "2，3",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Equating the two expressions gives $2x-1=-x+5$, so $3x=6$ and $x=2$. Substituting into $y=-x+5$ gives $y=3$. The intersection is $(2,3)$.",
